WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.567
-Testing!

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:02.668
-Okay. Quiet, please!

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:05.338
-This is Scene 50, take 1.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.672
Scene 50. Alright.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:10.776
♪♪

00:00:10.776 --> 00:00:13.112
-We're back in the building.
We're back in the studio.

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.614
And it's great.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.949
It gives us a lot of opportunity

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:20.286
to do more topical things
that we've been wanting to do.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.122
We did Harry Styles.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:26.626
We parodied Billie Eilish's
video hours after it came out.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:29.462
Even her people were like,
"How did you pull this off?"

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.631
It's our genius wardrobe
and our hair and makeup.

00:00:32.631 --> 00:00:34.300
Tonight, we're doing something,

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.636
the biggest thing
that we've done so far, I think,

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:38.137
as far as pulling something off.

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:40.206
We're spoofing "WandaVision."

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:43.042
-The writers came up with
"FallonVision,"

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:47.046
which was basically a fun way
for us to do some sets

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.382
that were historical
sort of talk shows.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:52.885
And so, we would bounce
through the ages

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:54.554
and we would have
different sets,

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.123
and Jimmy would be in different
costumes and all that stuff.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.558
-As long as
you're not thinking --

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.292
As long as you're not thinking
this man.

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:01.127
-Yeah.
-Know what I mean?

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.795
It's off of the man man.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:05.298
-Yeah.
-Then into a theater scene.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:07.600
And I think kind of look around
again, like, you know.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.634
Ha-ha!
-Yep.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.302
-This came together
super fast --

00:01:10.302 --> 00:01:11.638
three or four days.

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:13.139
We have very limited space,

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:16.408
so we madly drafted some things,
built it overnight,

00:01:16.408 --> 00:01:18.344
and just got it here
as quick as we could

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:21.513
and tried to kind of piece it
together to get the right look.

00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:24.583
-Ladies and gentlemen,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.352
Good evening.
I'm Jimmy Fallon,

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.021
broadcasting live in color
from Rock Center.

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:31.057
We back? Cool.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:34.060
Welcome back, guys.
I'm here with Elizabeth Olsen.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.562
The way I got into each
character before we did it

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:39.398
was very -- it was so fun.

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:42.569
Again, we're very lucky to have
great wardrobe and hair.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.570
But once you're in the wig,

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.240
or you can even see
on a little monitor

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.907
which is, you know, 20 feet away

00:01:48.907 --> 00:01:51.744
that it's black and white
and kind of kinescope-looking,

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:54.146
so your voice can be
very kind of stiff.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:55.147
-Action!

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:56.148
-Ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:57.484
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:59.185
Right now, I'm joined
by a lovely lady,

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.921
an actress by the name
of Miss Elizabeth Olsen.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:06.358
Then there's also decades where
people were, like, just smoking.

00:02:06.358 --> 00:02:09.195
Cigarettes. As a host.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:12.798
And I'm -- I do not
smoke cigarettes,

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:15.635
and so that was some really good
acting on my part.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.537
-What hand do you smoke with?
Left, right?

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.005
-Pssh!

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.674
Right, I guess? I don't smoke.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:25.010
-We had some smokers on the crew
that were just like...

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.880
"Guy. That is not how --
Oh, whatever."

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.249
I'm just, like, shaking.

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.418
You know, there's a '90s set.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.754
It's kind of a very
Conan O'Brien vibe,

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:37.423
where it's just, like,
wacky graphics.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:41.294
You know, at the time,
you know, it's normal.

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:43.462
We're here with
a crazy-talented actress.

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:47.300
You know her, you love her --
Lizzie Olsen, guys!

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.136
Uh, Liz, need a chill pill?

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.505
-We asked Elizabeth Olsen
would she be into

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:55.341
filming with us, like, a parody
where Jimmy travels through time

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.176
and she's always the guest
on the show.

00:02:57.176 --> 00:03:02.014
And she said yes, but she was
in London filming "Dr. Strange."

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:05.518
So we shipped her props
and wigs and costume,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.021
but it didn't get there in time,
so she basically --

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:11.190
here and her team shot it
by themselves,

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:15.161
then they sent a bunch of really
great footage on Monday.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:18.330
-So, our kind of secret
twist ending to this

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.500
is that it's all done
by Kathryn Hahn,

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.337
who plays Agnes
on "WandaVision."

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.505
Not only did she come through,

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.172
but, man, she came through!

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:30.676
Unbelievable pro,
and crushed it.

00:03:30.676 --> 00:03:31.844
[ Static ]

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:34.179
-But if it wasn't you,
then who was it?

00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:35.514
[ Static ]

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:39.352
-Ohh, poor Elizabeth.
[ Applause ]

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:42.055
-Wait. K-Kathryn Hahn?!
What are you doing here?

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.889
-What can I say?

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:46.059
TV just isn't
what it used to be.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.393
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.527
[ Ding ]

00:03:48.527 --> 00:03:51.030
-♪ Who's been messing up
everything? ♪

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:55.100
-♪ It's been Kathryn Hahn
all along ♪

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.436
-Alright. Good to see you guys.
Please stay safe and healthy.

00:03:57.436 --> 00:03:58.771
-You too.
-Likewise. Thank you again.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.039
-Bye!

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.208
-We love doing this.
We want to do more of this.

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:05.511
This was just the beginning
of what I think the potential

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:08.848
that we have to do
here at "The Tonight Show,"

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.684
even with limited resources
and a limited crew.

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:14.353
We're just gonna push ourselves.
We're all on the same team.

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:16.688
We want people to be like,
"How did they pull this off?"

00:04:16.688 --> 00:04:18.023
Especially in these times

00:04:18.023 --> 00:04:19.859
where we don't know
what's gonna happen,

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:22.762
we just want to make you happy
and we want to entertain people.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.764
And we're just getting going.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.065
Watch us.

